## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | js/unit-tests/run_ciDispatchPriority.json | 🚨 blocking canonical ci gate is red — the new suite never runs in ci and the module measures at 0 coverage the crap check fails on this pr s own head 0d3b3be2 and the failure is owned here ci classification json → class owned new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js unarm 42 new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js labelnames 30 new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js runage 30 new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js queuedunapprovedruns 30 new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js cancelrun 30 new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js otherapprovedruns 20 new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js predispatchskip 27 new 8 js sm cidispatchpriority js cancelbatch 8 7 0 regression s 8 new over threshold 0 improvement s 0 removed error process completed with exit code 2 root cause verified in the tree the coverage pass in github workflows quality yml 241 builds its test file list from js unit tests run all json → params jobparams testfiles and test cidispatchpriority js is not in that list — it is registered only in this new standalone run cidispatchpriority json which ci never loads consequences 1 all helpers of js sm cidispatchpriority js measure at 0 0 coverage in the ci pass → crap cc² cc → every function with cc ≥ 3 breaches the threshold 8 ratchet the log s crap table matches exactly 0 0 33 3 coverage on the flagged rows 2 the 15 new tests never execute in the canonical green gate — the module s dispatch cancel behavior ships effectively untested in ci despite the pr description claiming test coverage the pre commit gate passed locally because it runs the staged test files directly ci measures via run all json istanbul coverage the two disagreed and ci is the gate of record fix add js unit tests test cidispatchpriority js to js unit tests run all json s testfiles alphabetical slot keep the standalone run config with the suite covered crap for these helpers drops to ≤ cc all cc ≤ 8 gate is strictly 8 one caveat predispatchskip is cc 8 — it needs full branch coverage to stay ≤ 8 the existing tests already hit the verdict skip in flight skip different sha and throw paths but re run a local coverage pass to confirm no branch is left uncovered before pushing |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/sm/ciDispatchPriority.js | 💡 suggestion runs memo invalidation misses the stale cancel path — re dispatch after an in tick stale cancel defers one tick the module s contract header line 21 is one ci run listing per repo per tick memo reset by resettick and on every dispatch the invalidation has three cancel paths but only two drop the memo notedispatched line 276 → droprunsmemo ✓ after a dispatch aftermergeoutcome → droprunsmemo ✓ after the merge sweep cancelstaleandcureplaceholders → checkruncures cancelstaledispatchedruns — no memo drop ✗ that third path runs inside dispatchandarmvalidatepr immediately before predispatchskip sequence in one tick 1 gaterule s sweep populates runsmemo with the tick s active runs including a stale run on this branch sha 2 cancelstaledispatchedruns cancels that stale run — the memo still lists it as active 3 predispatchskip reads the memo sees the now cancelled run in flight on the same branch sha logs ⏭️ in flight ci already covers sha and marks the key handled — no re dispatch this tick though a cancelled run is explicitly not a verdict impact is bounded next tick resettick drops the memo and the cancelled run fails the isactive filter so the armed lane re dispatches the same sha net effect is a one tick defer where the old flow re dispatched in tick — consistent with this pr s defer heavy design hence a suggestion rather than a blocker fix drop the runs memo when the stale cancel path actually cancelled something — e g expose a small hook cidispatchprioritymodule droprunsmemo repoinfo is already exported adjacent and call it from cancelstaleandcureplaceholders when vcancelresult cancelled length 0 a one line test in test cidispatchpriority js pins it |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

